++diff --git a/fleet-patches/0011-server-disable-speculative-decoding-for-grammar-cons.patch b/fleet-patches/0011-server-disable-speculative-decoding-for-grammar-cons.patch
++new file mode 100644
++index 000000000..d2fde1ac3
++--- /dev/null
+++++ b/fleet-patches/0011-server-disable-speculative-decoding-for-grammar-cons.patch
++@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+++From 17ecd9d523571f62fce8d9c7bbc6adc7fe66f251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+++Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:50:19 -0500
+++Subject: [PATCH] server: disable speculative decoding for grammar-constrained
+++ requests
+++
+++Root cause (live-traced on gabesrv06, 2026-09-15): MTP speculative decoding
+++(--spec-type draft-mtp) corrupts grammar-constrained tool-call output. The
+++qwen3-coder tool-call template has several structurally-ambiguous decision
+++points (e.g. "keep emitting <parameter=...> template tags" vs "start the
+++actual argument value") where the model's own greedy pick is only narrowly
+++favored -- logit margins as low as ~0.03 observed live at these points, vs.
+++10+ at unambiguous positions. Batched-vs-sequential GPU execution numerical
+++differences (matches the already-known, upstream-closed #23335 "different
+++kernels for different batch sizes") are enough to tip these close calls, and
+++once tipped the model confidently continues down the wrong path, producing
+++runaway <parameter=...>/</function>/<tool_call> tag repetition. This
+++corrupts the JSON string content of a tool call's arguments because a
+++permissive JSON string-type grammar rule can't reject it -- it's
+++syntactically valid, just semantically wrong.
+++
+++Confirmed via direct live A/B on gabesrv06:
+++  - identical request, spec-decode off: 4/4 clean
+++  - identical request, spec-decode on (draft-mtp, with or without
+++    ngram-mod): reliably corrupted
+++  - checkpoint-restore-and-replay ruled out as the mechanism: traced a
+++    corrupted run end-to-end, zero restore events fired, every
+++    grammar-trigger/clone/copy event was textbook-correct
+++
+++This is not something our own draft-verification code can fix -- the
+++per-token sampling logic itself is correct (confirmed via full clone/copy
+++path review of common_sampler, llama_sampler_grammar, and
+++common_reasoning_budget), and greedy decoding through the speculative path
+++is supposed to be numerically exact. The divergence is in the underlying
+++batched-matmul kernel selection, not this fork's or upstream's control flow.
+++
+++Fix: disable drafting entirely (both ngram-mod and draft-mtp) for any
+++request with an active grammar (tool-calling, JSON-schema output, or a
+++user-supplied GBNF grammar) via get_n_draft_max(). Plain chat/completion
+++requests with no grammar keep the full speculative-decoding speed win
+++unaffected.
+++
+++See FLEET.md's "Known-fragile areas" and upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp#23577
+++(open, matches this failure family across CUDA/ROCm/Vulkan) / #23335
+++(closed as expected behavior -- the milder, already-mitigated version of
+++the same underlying phenomenon; this fleet already caps
+++--spec-draft-n-max at 2 for that).
+++
+++Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5
+++---
+++ tools/server/server-context.cpp | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
+++ 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)
+++
+++diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++index c4a533825..c859a7176 100644
+++--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
++++++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++@@ -487,6 +487,29 @@ struct server_slot {
+++             return 0;
+++         }
+++ 
++++        // Disable speculative decoding for grammar-constrained requests (tool-calling,
++++        // JSON-schema output, etc). Root-caused live on gabesrv06 (2026-09-15): under
++++        // MTP speculative decoding, the qwen3-coder tool-call template has several
++++        // structurally-ambiguous decision points (e.g. "keep emitting <parameter=...>
++++        // template tags" vs "start the actual argument value") where the model's own
++++        // greedy pick is only narrowly favored (margins as low as ~0.03 logits observed
++++        // live, vs. 10+ at unambiguous positions) -- batched-vs-sequential GPU execution
++++        // numerical differences are enough to tip these close calls, and once tipped the
++++        // model confidently continues down the wrong path, producing runaway
++++        // <parameter=.../</function>/<tool_call> tag-repetition that corrupts the JSON
++++        // string content a permissive string-type grammar rule can't reject (it's
++++        // syntactically valid, just semantically wrong). Not reproducible with
++++        // speculative decoding off; confirmed independent of ngram-mod (still corrupts
++++        // with only --spec-type draft-mtp). See FLEET.md's "Known-fragile areas" and
++++        // upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp#23577 (open, matches this failure family) /
++++        // #23335 (closed as expected: "different kernels for different batch sizes" --
++++        // the milder, already-mitigated version of the same underlying phenomenon).
++++        // Plain chat/completion requests (no grammar) keep the full speculative-decoding
++++        // speed win.
++++        if (task->params.sampling.grammar.type != COMMON_GRAMMAR_TYPE_NONE) {
++++            return 0;
++++        }
++++
