++From a1b3b4199f379ebcc105fe75d499db21bd637ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:36:23 -0500
++Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: occupancy-aware S/M/L tile selector for non-coopmat2
++ path (AMD/Intel)
++
++The non-coopmat2 tile-shape selector (AMD RDNA / Intel int-dot/MMQ path,
++ggml_vk_guess_matmul_pipeline/_id_pipeline's device->matmul_tile_selector/
++matmul_id_tile_selector lambdas) picked S/M/L purely from static m/n
++thresholds, unlike the coopmat2 branch, which weighs tile count against
++shader_core_count to avoid under-occupying the GPU. Ports that same
++tiles_l/tiles_m-vs-shader_core_count math into the non-coopmat2 branch,
++gated on shader_core_count != 0 so behavior is unchanged when that data
++isn't available. Applies to any non-coopmat2 AMD/Intel Vulkan device.
++
++LLAMA_VK_TILE_OCCUPANCY=0 forces the old static-threshold behavior for
++A/B testing.
++
++Verified via test-backend-ops (MUL_MAT 1148/1148, MUL_MAT_ID 921/921) on
++an NVIDIA dev GPU and on gabesrv10 (Radeon 8060S/RADV GFX1151, 40 CU) --
++correct on both. Live A/B on gabesrv10 (llama-bench, production model,
++large prefill + boundary M/N shapes) showed no repeatable difference vs.
++the static thresholds at that CU count -- both heuristics pick the same
++tile for nearly every real shape there. Canarying on gabesrv06 (Radeon
++780M/gfx1103, 12 CU) to check whether a much lower CU count is where this
++actually diverges.
++
++Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
